  "Question": "If \\(p\\ge5\\) is a prime number, then \\(24\\) divides \\(p^2-1\\) without remainder",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "never",
    "B": "sometimes only",
    "C": "always",
    "D": "only if \\(p=5\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Factoring reveals two nearby integers whose divisibility is easy to track:\n\\[\np^2-1=(p-1)(p+1).\n\\]\nA prime \\(p\\ge5\\) is divisible by neither \\(2\\) nor \\(3\\). In particular, \\(p\\) is odd, so \\(p-1\\) and \\(p+1\\) are consecutive even integers. One is divisible by \\(4\\), and the other is divisible by \\(2\\). Their product is therefore divisible by \\(8\\).\n\nAmong the three consecutive integers \\(p-1,p,p+1\\), exactly one is divisible by \\(3\\). It cannot be \\(p\\), so one of the two factors \\(p-1\\) and \\(p+1\\) is divisible by \\(3\\). Their product is thus divisible by \\(3\\) as well as \\(8\\).\n\nThe least common multiple of \\(3\\) and \\(8\\) is \\(24\\), so \\(24\\) divides \\(p^2-1\\) for every allowed prime. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{always}}\\), choice C.",
